| ---- Rule Metadata ----
| Rule Name: Brute Force to Successful Login
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 (Credential Access — Brute Force)
| Severity: High
| Description: Detects 5+ failed logins followed by a successful login from the same source IP within 10 minutes
| Author: Vignesh R
| Created: YYYY-MM-DD
| ---- Search Logic ----

index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security"
    (EventCode=4625 OR EventCode=4624)
| eval event_type=if(EventCode=4625, "failure", "success")
| stats
    count(eval(event_type="failure")) AS failed_count
    count(eval(event_type="success")) AS success_count
    earliest(_time) AS first_event
    latest(_time) AS last_event
    values(TargetUserName) AS targeted_accounts
    BY Source_Network_Address
| where failed_count >= 5 AND success_count >= 1
| eval time_window_minutes = round((last_event - first_event) / 60, 2)
| where time_window_minutes <= 10
| eval severity="HIGH"
| table Source_Network_Address, targeted_accounts, failed_count, success_count, time_window_minutes, severity, first_event, last_event

| ---- Alert Configuration ----
| Schedule: Every 10 minutes
| Alert condition: Number of results > 0
| Alert action: Create TheHive case, send webhook notification
| Throttle: 1 hour per Source_Network_Address

| ---- Tuning Notes ----
| - Adjust failed_count threshold based on environment baseline
| - Add whitelist for known jump servers or VPN concentrators
| - Consider excluding service accounts with known automated retry behaviour
| - Monitor for distributed brute force (same target, multiple sources) separately
